{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the stuck `orders-validator` consumer and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200.\n\n- **Cause:** `orders-validator` stopped at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` topic on a malformed JSON record. It paused there permanently, so nothing after that offset was processed.\n- **Fix:** I edited the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap so a bad record is sent to a new `orders-fulfillment-dlq` topic. The offset is then committed and processing continues. I restarted the deployment.\n- **Result:** The consumer went past offset 20 and was processing new orders normally at offset 48 when I last checked.\n\nI did not look at the frontend, traces or request latency, and I didn't confirm that end-user requests recovered. I took `orders-validator` as the cause because it was the only component logging errors. All pods are Running."}}
